WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:03.960
The upcoming "Knives Out"&nbsp;
sequel has another stacked cast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:09.240
but it's the surprise cameos that are sure&nbsp;
to get people talking. Who shows up? Will the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:13.380
film be darker than the first? Here's all&nbsp;
you need to know before the big premiere.

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:19.560
In November 2019, writer and director Rian&nbsp;
Johnson made waves with his murder-mystery&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:25.200
film "Knives Out." The acclaimed whodunnit earned&nbsp;
rave reviews and raked in a seriously impressive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:30.660
pull at the box office against a relatively modest&nbsp;
budget, which is saying nothing of its multiple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:35.640
Golden Globe nominations. Luckily for all the&nbsp;
legions of "Knives Out" fans out there, neither&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:40.920
Craig nor Johnson hesitated to express their&nbsp;
interest in revisiting detective Benoit Blanc.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:46.020
In fact, during a pre-Golden Globes&nbsp;
party held by Lionsgate in January 2020,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:50.340
Johnson told The Hollywood Reporter that&nbsp;
he was already working on a script for a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:53.640
"Knives Out" sequel. Following the&nbsp;
world premiere of "Glass Onion" at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:57.960
the 2022 Toronto International Film&nbsp;
Festival, Johnson remarked that he'll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:03.120
keep making "Knives Out" sequels for as long&nbsp;
as his star lets him. Via Variety, he joked,

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:06.610
"I'm going to keep making these&nbsp;
until Daniel blocks me on his phone."

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:09.070
"It sounds crazy, but it'll work."

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:13.440
However, despite how much he clearly&nbsp;
enjoys making his Craig-led whodunnits,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:17.580
Johnson did tell the Los Angeles Times&nbsp;
that he found writing "Glass Onion" to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:20.700
be a particularly difficult&nbsp;
experience. Johnson shared,

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:24.840
"It was scary. I also spent 10 years&nbsp;
planning 'Knives Out,' whereas this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:26.760
I was kind of starting from scratch."

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:31.260
Fortunately, if the film's overwhelmingly&nbsp;
positive early reviews are any indication,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:36.291
it looks like Johnson already has the excuses he&nbsp;
needs to keep making his "Knives Out" sequels.

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:42.060
The main creative team members behind "Knives&nbsp;
Out" began working on a sequel only a few months&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:45.780
after the film's release. So, it shouldn't&nbsp;
come as much of a surprise to learn that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:50.640
"Glass Onion: A Knives Out Mystery" is set to&nbsp;
be released relatively shortly. For his part,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:54.240
Daniel Craig likely had a little more&nbsp;
time to spare for "Glass Onion," too,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:59.520
given the fact that his tenure as James Bond&nbsp;
came to an end in 2021 with "No Time to Die."

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:03.780
All of which is to say that "Knives Out" fans&nbsp;
don't have to wait much longer to see the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:09.480
follow-up to that beloved 2019 whodunnit. Indeed,&nbsp;
"Glass Onion" is currently set to premiere Friday,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:14.640
December 23 on Netflix. Rian Johnson also&nbsp;
announced on Twitter in early October&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:19.080
that "Glass Onion" will be released in select&nbsp;
theaters one month prior to its late December&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:24.060
Netflix premiere. That means "Knives Out" fans&nbsp;
will get the chance to see "Glass Onion" early,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:28.680
though, the film is only set to play in&nbsp;
theaters throughout the week of November 23.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.840
"Glass Onion: A Knives Out Mystery" will&nbsp;
tell a completely different story than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:39.180
its predecessor. According to Netflix's TUDUM,&nbsp;
Rian Johnson's "Knives Out" sequel will be set&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:43.680
in the Mediterranean and will follow Edward&nbsp;
Norton's tech billionaire Miles Bron and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:47.580
friends he invites to his private island in&nbsp;
Greece. As you might have already guessed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:51.360
one of these friends ends up dead, and&nbsp;
it's Daniel Craig's Benoit Blanc who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:55.020
is ultimately tasked with discovering&nbsp;
the identity of the victim's murderer.

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:58.560
As was the case in "Knives Out," the&nbsp;
new film's wealthy central characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:01.860
will all be far from perfect.&nbsp;
While speaking with TUDUM,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:05.880
Johnson even touched on the relationships&nbsp;
at the center of "Glass Onion," saying,

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:08.580
"It's structured around a&nbsp;
group of friends, or frenemies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:13.200
who all have a power dynamic with one of their&nbsp;
successful friends. It begins with him sending&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:17.400
an invitation for them to come and play this&nbsp;
murder mystery game at this exotic locale."

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:20.820
Fans will, unfortunately, have to&nbsp;
wait to find out not only who the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:25.260
key victim is in "Glass Onion" but who is&nbsp;
ultimately responsible for their death.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:26.400
"Really, dude?"

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.361
"Oh my god."

00:03:28.361 --> 00:03:29.310
"Really."

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:34.200
"Knives Out" boasted some pretty impressive&nbsp;
star power. In addition to Daniel Craig,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:40.080
the film's cast included heavy hitters like&nbsp;
Ana de Armas, Jamie Lee Curtis, Toni Collette,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:48.300
Chris Evans, Don Johnson, Jaeden Martell, Michael&nbsp;
Shannon, Katherine Langford, and Riki Lindhome.

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:51.180
LaKeith Stanfield also turned&nbsp;
in a memorable performance in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:53.460
"Knives Out" as Detective Lieutenant Elliot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:58.440
while Noah Segan made a lasting impression&nbsp;
as Trooper Wagner. Fortunately, "Glass Onion:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:03.240
A Knives Out Mystery" seems to have assembled&nbsp;
a similarly impressive ensemble of actors.

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:08.820
Not only will "Glass Onion" center, once again,&nbsp;
around Craig's Benoit Blanc but the long-awaited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:14.220
"Knives Out" sequel will also introduce viewers&nbsp;
to a new lineup of eccentric characters. Indeed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:17.580
while no "Knives Out" cast members&nbsp;
outside of Craig are expected to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:21.780
appear in "Glass Onion," the new film's&nbsp;
cast does feature recognizable stars.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:28.140
This includes Kate Hudson, Edward Norton,&nbsp;
Kathryn Hahn, Dave Bautista, Ethan Hawke,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:32.160
Madelyn Cline, Jessica Henwick, Leslie Odom Jr.,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:37.440
and Janelle Monáe. Plus — spoiler alert for&nbsp;
what will likely be fun cameos — the film will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:43.260
mark the final on-screen appearances of two late&nbsp;
legends: Stephen Sondheim and Angela Lansbury.

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:46.860
In other words, it seems safe to&nbsp;
say that "Glass Onion" has managed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:51.210
to successfully steal, at the very least,&nbsp;
one page from its predecessor's playbook.

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:55.980
"Glass Onion: A Knives Out Story" is,&nbsp;
just like the original "Knives Out" was,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.980 --> 00:05:01.920
rated PG-13. The film's rating is reportedly&nbsp;
due to strong language, drug content,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:06.870
some violence, and sexual material. Taking&nbsp;
that into account, it sounds like "Glass&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:10.740
Onion" will be a bit edgier and more mature&nbsp;
than some parents may be comfortable with.

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:16.860
For whatever it's worth, 2019's "Knives Out" was&nbsp;
rated PG-13 for drug material, brief violence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:22.080
sexual references, some strong language, and&nbsp;
thematic elements. In other words, it sounds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:26.340
like "Glass Onion" will have worse language&nbsp;
and sexual references than "Knives Out" did.

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:30.300
Whether or not "Glass Onion" ends up&nbsp;
being considerably darker in tone and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:33.960
content than "Knives Out," however,&nbsp;
remains to be seen. Parents should,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:38.760
nonetheless, note the differences between the&nbsp;
two films' PG-13 ratings if they're debating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.760 --> 00:05:42.420
whether or not to take their kids to&nbsp;
see "Glass Onion" later this year.

